  "id": "COMPOUND:18648 - PROTEIN:5790",
  "verbalization": "Nigrolineaxanthone F is implicated in the interaction with HPAC through a series of molecular pathways involving dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family members. The evidence suggests that Nigrolineaxanthone F acts as a target for multiple enzymes, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn targets HPAC. This indicates a potential mechanism where Nigrolineaxanthone F may modulate HPAC activity through the enzymatic pathways it interacts with. The presence of multiple targets, including Phorone and Propamidine, further supports a broader role of Nigrolineaxanthone F in influencing HPAC, possibly through different metabolic routes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction, emphasizing the importance of SDR family members in mediating the effects of Nigrolineaxanthone F on HPAC.",
